			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite/113200798595762520",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jared White (ResistanceNet ✊)",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/552/988/169/598/original/863bd81d9ad9d7b6.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-09-25T23:31:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> ah, a docs PR!</p><p>I'm not sure how you like to tackle that stuff, but I've come to discover it's so-o-o much easier to document new features in its own docs PR than co-located with code (Bridgetown’s a monorepo). I used to think I should try to write docs as if it's part of a checklist along with tests and other code-level concerns, and that really gunked up the works.</p><p>Anyways…just curious!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113203933101502639",
			"parentId": "113200798628079982",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/113203933101502639",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-09-26T12:48:56.242Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jaredwhite</span></a></span> I try really hard to maintain only one live/latest branch of docs—but some of this ESM stuff was too intrusive to live on `www` before `v3` shipped stable—thus the PR. Lots of v3 features are already documented on `www` right now!</p><p>I used to go nuts with versioned docs for every minor release but now I’m planning on just doing major release subdomains moving forward: <a href=\"https://www.11ty.dev/docs/versions/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">11ty.dev/docs/versions/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
